<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      type="topic" id="help-viewer">
  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#start"/>
    <title type="sort">2</title>
    <link type="seealso" xref="keyboard-shortcuts"/>
    <desc>Go back, search the help, find words on a page, make the text
    larger, and print a page.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Reading this help</title>

  <p>The help opens in Yelp, the help viewer that comes with GNOME,
  Cinnamon and MATE. Where Yelp is not installed, LinuxZPL opens it in a
  help viewer of its own, which looks and works the same way. Either way
  there is one help window: <gui>Help</gui> in another window shows that
  window's page in it. The help window stays open after LinuxZPL is
  closed.</p>

  <section id="moving">
    <title>Moving around</title>
    <p>Click a blue link to go to that page. The line at the top of a page
    leads back to its part of the contents, and the foot of a page lists
    the contents' part again under <gui>More Information</gui> and related
    pages under <gui>See Also</gui>. <gui>Back</gui> and <gui>Forward</gui>,
    the arrows at the left of the title, go back to the pages you came
    through, each where you left it. In LinuxZPL's own viewer,
    <guiseq><gui>Menu</gui><gui>Contents</gui></guiseq> goes to the
    contents.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="search">
    <title>Searching the help</title>
    <p>Click the search button, type some words and press
    <key>Enter</key>. The pages holding every word are listed, those with
    the words in their title first. Click one to open it, at the part of
    the page the words are in.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="find">
    <title>Finding words on this page</title>
    <p><guiseq><gui>Menu</gui><gui>Find…</gui></guiseq> opens a find bar.
    Type the words and every place they are on the page is marked, with the
    page scrolled to the first. In LinuxZPL's own viewer the bar is below
    the page: <key>Enter</key> or the down arrow goes to the next place,
    <keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq> or the up arrow to
    the one before, and <key>Escape</key> closes the bar.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="size">
    <title>Larger text</title>
    <p><guiseq><gui>Menu</gui><gui>Larger Text</gui></guiseq> and
    <gui>Smaller Text</gui> change the size of the pages' text. LinuxZPL's
    own viewer remembers the size for the next time it opens.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="print">
    <title>Printing a page</title>
    <p><guiseq><gui>Menu</gui><gui>Print…</gui></guiseq> in LinuxZPL's own
    viewer opens the page as a PDF in your PDF viewer, to print from
    there. Making the PDFs takes a few seconds the first time. With no PDF
    viewer installed, a message says where the PDF is.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="keys">
    <title>Keys</title>
    <p>These are Yelp's keys, and LinuxZPL's own viewer has the same.</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><td><p>Keys</p></td><td><p>Does</p></td></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>Left</key></keyseq>, <keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>Right</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Back, Forward</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>S</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Search the help</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>F</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Find words on this page</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>+</key></keyseq>, <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>-</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Larger text, smaller text</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Print the page</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>W</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>Close the help</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><keyseq><key>Alt</key><key>Home</key></keyseq></p></td><td><p>The contents (LinuxZPL's own viewer)</p></td></tr>
        <tr><td><p><key>F1</key></p></td><td><p>This page (LinuxZPL's own viewer)</p></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</page>
